        "title": "Hindu Mythology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Hindu mythology is not a single tradition — it is the accumulated theological production of one of the world's oldest continuous civilizations, spanning roughly 3,500 years from the Rigveda (~1500 BCE) to the living tradition today. It is encyclopedic: 18 major Puranas, two massive epics (the Mahabharata alone is 10× the Iliad and Odyssey combined), countless Upanishads and Tantric texts."
